              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How much does a Landice L7 treadmill cost?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                On 5 November 2026 Landice listed the residential L7 from $5,429 with the Pro Sports console and standard belt to $7,804 with the Elite touchscreen, orthopedic belt and TV mount. The Achieve console version was $5,929. Dealer prices and promotions can differ.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the difference between the Landice L7 and L8?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                The L8 has a 22 by 63-inch running area instead of 20 by 58, a 500 lb rating instead of 400, and a 35 by 83-inch footprint instead of 35 by 76. Motor rating, speed, incline and consoles are the same. On 5 November 2026 it cost $900 to $1,000 more than an L7 with the same console.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the Landice L7 RTM?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                The rehabilitation version of the L7. It adds extended medical handrails, a very low starting speed, an optional reversing belt with remote stop/start and an electrical isolation kit. On 5 November 2026 Landice listed it from $5,429 to $6,829, with five years of parts cover.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the Landice L890CT?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                We could not find the code on any current listing. Landice’s codes combine the model and console (L890PST, L890AT), so L890CT most likely means an L8 with the older Cardio Trainer console, which Landice no longer offers. Any L890CT for sale now is used, remanufactured or old stock.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What mounts are available for the Landice L7?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Landice sells a tablet mount for 7- to 12-inch tablets ($75) and a TV or monitor mount ($250), as options on the L7 or as separate accessories, and an $800 Landice Vision System. The RTM can be ordered with a 19-inch HDTV and mount.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can you buy a Landice L7 on Amazon?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                We could not find it sold new on Amazon. Landice sells through its own online store and specialty fitness dealers, and accepts HSA and FSA payment.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div class="mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes Buying a Landice L7</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The L7 is expensive enough that small errors cost real money. These are the ones to avoid.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Comparing base prices instead of configurations</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The L7 runs from $5,429 to $7,804 depending on console, belt and mount. Compare the same configuration across Landice and dealers, and against rivals.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying the L7 when you need the L8 deck</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">A 58-inch deck is short for tall runners. If you are over about six feet and run, the L8’s 63-inch deck is the reason to pay $900 more.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming every Landice warranty is lifetime</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The residential L7 lists lifetime parts, but the RTM lists five years and a dealer listing shows five years. Get the terms for your exact version and installation in writing.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Not measuring the delivery route</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The L7 does not fold, is 76 inches long and ships at 345 lb. Measure doors, stairs and turns before ordering, and confirm who installs it.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

